The Principal Developer will have a technical focus on enabling the notification platform for customer travel. This role will lead efforts to design, develop, and maintain innovative solutions while collaborating with portfolio owners and service providers.
The Principal Developer plays a critical role in maintaining the strategic partnership between business needs and technology delivery. This individual will apply strong communication, analytical, and critical-thinking skills to identify, communicate, and resolve issues, opportunities, and problems to maximize IT and business investments.
The Principal Developer has decision-making authority, works independently with minimal supervision, and mentors and coaches others. This individual has extensive knowledge and experience across multiple technologies and business areas.
• Define and implement technical solutions for new systems or enhance existing systems using modern technologies.
• Define technical service-level agreements (SLAs) and data-sharing strategies with vendors.
• Lead the design, development, and planning of solutions and technology standards to solve complex business problems.
• Perform hands-on development and support software systems by optimizing performance, resolving problems, and following up on issues and solutions.
• Ensure systems are properly integrated.
• Partner with business, support, and development teams to recommend system enhancements.
• Serve as a resource for technology and project development reviews and technical assessments.
• Ensure technical solutions meet customers' business goals.
• Provide consultation and technical leadership throughout project lifecycle planning.
• Ensure consistency and adherence to enterprise standards and guiding principles throughout the application lifecycle.
• Identify opportunities to leverage and influence existing infrastructure and application components.
• Monitor industry trends through benchmarking, professional associations, and other activities to advise others on strategic technology direction.
• Provide feedback to enterprise technology owners and architects regarding future solution needs.
• Apply the enterprise vision and strategy to project solutions while balancing tactical delivery needs.
• Partner with business and IT collaborators to define the domain architecture strategy.
• Demonstrate mastery of development domain areas, multiple technologies, and toolsets.
• Demonstrate mastery of software engineering.
• Maintain accountability for PCI and SOX environments and development.

